# Phase 3 Step 3.2: pin line endings for files where the lock-integrity CI
# job compares committed bytes against newly regenerated bytes.
#
# pip-compile writes lock files using the host OS line ending (CRLF on Windows,
# LF on Linux). Without this attribute, git's autocrlf could rewrite line
# endings during checkout, causing tools/diff_locks.py to report spurious
# whole-file diffs. We pin requirements*.lock to LF so the source-of-truth
# representation in the repo is OS-independent. The lock-integrity job
# regenerates with the same LF convention on Windows via Git Bash's pip-compile.
requirements*.lock text eol=lf
